      "writtenOn": "2023-11-30T09:18:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The original RA daemon used to sleep a thread for a specific period to schedule multicasts. If the device went to sleep, the thread wouldn\u0027t wake up, which meant that the scheduling period wasn\u0027t guaranteed. This introduced a multicast RA timer correctness issue, but it also meant that the RA daemon wouldn\u0027t hold the wakelock.\nThe new design uses WakeMessage. From the docs, WakeMessage will wake up system when it try to send the specified message to a Handler and keeps the system awake until the message is processed.\nI remember while we talked about his change, you had some test system wakeup. Could you mention your tests and results in the commit message to warrant the change?",
      "revId": "d46c0850ac572836aa0e9b8bb4e1d264450e57ca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
