      "writtenOn": "2023-11-30T09:18:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the past, the RA daemon only scheduled multicast when it had an RA to send. Now, it schedules multicast when it starts up and reschedules the timer when the old timer expires. But what happens if you\u0027re on an IPv4-only network? In that case, the RA daemon will keep scheduling timers even though it doesn\u0027t have an RA to send. That seems like a waste of resources.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 295,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 295,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "d46c0850ac572836aa0e9b8bb4e1d264450e57ca",
