      "writtenOn": "2023-11-30T09:18:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Before, MulticastTransmitter could use thread sleep to loop the timer scheduling. This was fine because it didn\u0027t wake up the system. Now you\u0027ve changed it to use WakeupMessage, which will actually wake up the system when it tries to send a message. We need to be careful to only schedule the timer when necessary. In particular, we need to cancel the timer when the RaParams object is null.",
